# row-group-key-logical.rq (loop N, AXIOM) — the group KEY for one aggregation row confirmed
# over the LOGICAL table (a continuation chain), whose member rows may sit on several pages.
#
# THE SAME LAW as row-group-key.rq, over a BIGGER HOLON. The key is still the unique distinct
# non-blank cellText in the LABEL COLUMN among the member rows (?agg tab:aggregates ?m), and
# uniqueness is still a query-local NOT EXISTS — a holon-scoped closed-world guard inside an
# open derivation (§8). What grows is the holon the guard closes over: the page-local table
# becomes the logical table the pagination cut, so a member on page 2 is read by the same rule
# as a member on page 0. No unique value -> zero rows -> NO group (honest refusal, §7).
#
# WHY IT CANNOT SIMPLY BIND ?lcol: each member table mints its OWN column nodes, so "the label
# column" is a DIFFERENT URI on every page of the chain. The correspondence is not guessed and
# not parsed out of the IRIs — it is the asserted tab:continuesColumn link, licensed by clauses
# (b)+(c) of continuation-of.rq (column-for-column in both directions = a bijection at equal
# index). ?lcol is bound to the HEAD table's column; `tab:continuesColumn*` reaches it from any
# member's column, at any depth, and its ZERO-length case covers the head's own cells.
#
# ORDER BY ?pg ?y picks the author's FIRST writing of the key in READING order — page first,
# then the cell's tab:y0 within the page. y0 alone is page-local and would let a page-2 cell
# outrank a page-0 one. tab:onPage is REQUIRED, not OPTIONAL: this query runs only over a
# compiled document graph, where every tab:EntryCell carries its page; a cell without one would
# make the ordering arbitrary, and refusing is the safe direction (§7).
#
# Bindings: ?agg = the tab:DetectedAggregationRow URI; ?lcol = the HEAD table's label column.
# The aggregation row's own label text is never read (no language matching).
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
SELECT ?v ?cell WHERE {
  ?agg tab:aggregates ?m .
  ?cell a tab:EntryCell ; tab:atRow ?m ; tab:atColumn ?mc ; tab:cellText ?v ;
        tab:onPage ?pg ; tab:hasBBox ?bb .
  ?mc tab:continuesColumn* ?lcol .
  ?bb tab:y0 ?y .
  FILTER(STR(?v) != "")
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?agg tab:aggregates ?m2 .
    ?c2 a tab:EntryCell ; tab:atRow ?m2 ; tab:atColumn ?mc2 ; tab:cellText ?v2 .
    ?mc2 tab:continuesColumn* ?lcol .
    FILTER(STR(?v2) != "" && STR(?v2) != STR(?v))
  }
}
ORDER BY ?pg ?y
LIMIT 1
